red electric generation facilities. The company was incorporated in 1995 and is based in Oakland, California.","ceo_bio":"Ms. Patricia Kessler Poppe | CEO & Director | Age 56 | Compensation: $8.6M (FY2025)","culture_narrative":"Employs approximately 29K people. Revenue per employee of $860K ranks in the below the sector median among Utilities peers. Stock-based compensation of $5K per employee reflects an ownership culture. CEO compensation is 10\u00d7 revenue per employee (reasonable relative to workforce productivity). Governance score flags elevated compensation governance risk (8/10).","financial_summary":["Pacific Gas & Electric Co. is a large-cap utilities business with a $28.6B market cap on $24.9B of annual revenue.","The top line has compounded at +5% over the past three years and +4% annually across the full decade, which puts it in mature, slow-growth territory.","Returns on capital run at 3% against a 6% cost of capital, which means the business is destroying value with every dollar it reinvests.","The company is burning through $3.1B of cash, and without positive owner earnings any valuation rests on hope rather than evidence.","On the balance sheet, debt is heavy at 12.7\u00d7 net debt/EBITDA, and leverage like that is what turns a bad year into a permanent loss, and thin 1.6\u00d7 interest coverage leaves no room for a bad year.","Shareholder yield is only 1.5%, a thin return of capital, and insider ownership is negligible, so management has little personal stake in the long-term outcome."],"sector_headwinds":[{"text":"Price sits 33% above estimated fair value \u2014 no margin of safety left, and the cushion against estimate error has been bid away","sev":"red","cat":"valuation","magnitude":0.3250972942875667},{"text":"Piotroski score 3/9 \u2014 the fundamentals are deteriorating on multiple fronts","sev":"red","cat":"quality"},{"text":"Altman Z in the distress zone (0.4) \u2014 the kind of balance-sheet risk that can make a loss permanent","sev":"red","cat":"quality"},{"text":"Volatile returns on capital suggest the moat is narrower than a snapshot ROIC implies","sev":"amber","cat":"moat"},{"text":"Insiders are net sellers (80% sell ratio, net $3.4M) \u2014 the people closest to the business are reducing their personal stake","sev":"amber","cat":"insider"},{"text":"ROIC sits in the bottom quartile among Utilities peers \u2014 no moat advantage to speak of","sev":"amber","cat":"moat"},{"text":"Carries more leverage than most Utilities peers \u2014 a smaller cushion for the inevitable bad year","sev":"amber","cat":"balance_sheet"},{"text":"Financial quality metrics lag Utilities peers","sev":"amber","cat":"quality"},{"text":"Above-average market volatility (VIX 26)","sev":"amber","cat":"macro"},{"text":"Wildfire and climate liability \u2014 extreme weather events create catastrophic, uninsurable losses that can push even investment-grade utilities toward restructuring.","sev":"amber","cat":"thesis_risk"}],"sector_tailwinds":["Trading near the bottom of its 52-week range \u2014 the market is offering a discount","Valued at a 29% discount to sector median EV/EBITDA","Healthy payout ratio leaves room for both dividend growth and reinvestment","Utilities sector outperforming the broader market over the past quarter","Utilities tends to hold up well as investors rotate into defensive names"],"news_headlines":[{"title":"PG&E (PCG) Stock Could Be 43% Overvalued Despite Wildfire Liability Push","source":"simplywall.st","link":"https://simplywall.st/stocks/us/utilities/nyse-pcg/pge/news/pge-pcg-stock-could-be-43-overvalued-despite-wildfire-liabil","date":"2026-11-05","timestamp":1793875469.735,"origin":"tiingo","sentiment":0.658,"tier":0,"scope":"company","tags":[]},{"title":"Can PG&E (NYSE:PCG) Keep Its Guidance After A Softer Quarter?","source":"kalkinemedia.com","link":"https://kalkinemedia.com/us/stocks/utility/can-pge-nysepcg-keep-its-guidance-after-a-softer-quarter","date":"2026-11-05","timestamp":1793839320.0,"orig